UPDATE public.people SET summary = 'Allaudin Shah, also known as Jam Juna I, was the second and fourth Sultan of Sindh, by succession. He belonged to the Sammā dynasty, reigning (r. 1352–1368, 1371–1389) first as a diarch alongside Jam Banbina II and later as sole monarch.' WHERE id = 'jam-juna-ii-1428-samma';
UPDATE public.people SET summary = 'Jam Nizamuddin II, also known as Jam Nindo, was the sixteenth Sultan of Sindh from Sammā dynasty, reigning from 1461 to 1508. His reign, the longest in the dynasty''s history, saw the expansion of the Samma Sultanate, the growth of Thatta as a centre of trade and learning, and sustained military and diplomatic relations with neighbouring states.' WHERE id = 'jam-nizam-1404-samma';
UPDATE public.people SET summary = 'Sadruddin II Shah, also known as Sikandar I Shah or Jam Sikandar I, was the tenth Sultan of Sindh from the Juna branch of the Samma dynasty. He reigned from 1412 to 1413, succeeding his brother Jam Karan.' WHERE id = 'jam-sikandar-i-1412-samma';
